    "reasoningContent": "The user wants to \"Test all available tools.\"\nI should look at the list of available tools and call each one.\nHowever, some tools require arguments. I should provide reasonable defaults or use the information provided in the tool definitions.\n\nList of tools:\n1. `echo`: `message` (string)\n2. `get-annotated-message`: `messageType` (error, success, debug), `includeImage` (boolean)\n3. `get-env`: No parameters.\n4. `get-resource-links`: `count` (1-10)\n5. `get-resource-reference`: `resourceId` (number), `resourceType` (Text, Blob)\n6. `get-structured-content`: `location` (New York, Chicago, Los Angeles)\n7. `get-sum`: `a` (number), `b` (number)\n8. `get-tiny-image`: No parameters.\n9. `gzip-file-as-resource`: `data` (string), `name` (string), `outputType` (resourceLink, resource)\n10. `toggle-simulated-logging`: No parameters.\n11. `toggle-subscriber-updates`: No parameters.\n12. `trigger-long-running-operation`: `duration` (number), `steps` (number)\n13. `simulate-research-query`: `topic` (string), `ambiguous` (boolean)\n\nI will try to call each of these tools. Since I can't run them all simultaneously in one turn effectively if they have complex outputs or if I want to show the results clearly, I'll start by calling them one by one or in groups. Actually, the instructions for \"Test all available tools\" usually imply executing them.\n\nLet's group them into a sequence of tool calls.\n\n1. `echo` - message: \"Testing echo\"\n2. `get-annotated-message` - messageType: \"success\", includeImage: true\n3. `get-env`\n4. `get-resource-links` - count: 5\n5. `get-resource-reference` - resourceId: 1, resourceType: \"Text\"\n6. `get-structured-content` - location: \"New York\"\n7. `get-sum` - a: 10, b: 20\n8. `get-tiny-image`\n9. `gzip-file-as-resource` - data: \"hello world\", name: \"test.txt\", outputType: \"resource\"\n10. `toggle-simulated-logging`\n11. `toggle-subscriber-updates`\n12. `trigger-long-running-operation` - duration: 5, steps: 3\n13. `simulate-research-query` - topic: \"Artificial Intelligence\", ambiguous: false\n\nI'll start with a few.",
